# {% project_name %}

A [Soroban](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/smart-contracts) smart
contract for the Stellar network, generated by
[Lumenprint](https://github.com/LumenAnvil/lumenprint).

This is the owner/admin starting point: one privileged address may change
protected state and hand over control, while reads stay open to everyone.

## The pattern

Two details do the real work, and both are easy to get wrong:

- **The admin is set in `__constructor`.** The host runs it atomically with
  deployment, so the contract is never live without an admin. A separate
  `initialize` function that anyone may call first is a well-known way to lose a
  contract in the gap between deploying and configuring it.
- **Privileged functions call `require_auth`.** That makes the host verify a
  signature from the stored admin. Taking an `Address` argument and comparing it
  against the admin proves nothing, because the caller chooses the argument.

`transfer_admin` is a direct, one-step transfer. If it is handed an address
nobody controls, the contract becomes unadministrable — production contracts
often use a two-step transfer where the incoming admin must accept first.

